=> Install Ansible

Ansible's documentation provides an Ubuntu installation through the Ansible PPA.

Run these commands one by one:

a) sudo apt install software-properties-common -y

Then:

b) sudo add-apt-repository --yes --update ppa:ansible/ansible

Then:

c) sudo apt install ansible -y

That's it. Ansible should now be installed.

=> Check Ansible

Run:

ansible --version

You should see something similar to:

ansible [core ...]
  config file = ...
  python version = ...

The exact version may be different.

=> Test Ansible locally

Since you currently have only WSL/Ubuntu, let's first test Ansible against the same Ubuntu machine.

Run:

ansible localhost -m ping

You should get something similar to:

localhost | SUCCESS => {
    "changed": false,
    "ping": "pong"
}

This means:

Ansible
   ↓
localhost (your WSL Ubuntu)
   ↓
SUCCESS

So Ansible is working 
